{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f7eaadcb-e41d-4c10-b34f-efcf1c42407c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6477bb4a998f9fb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-dvla9gvh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving parity\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators reaches functional and performance parity with the productized CUDA builds for the platform's supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware and produces the parity data plus a recommended go/no-go productization scope per model — the outcome that determines the scope of the vLLM ROCm serving runtime productization. The epic's scope also includes securing access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab arrangement).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct hardware for the campaign (procurement or partner-lab); the granting of access is externally controlled and tracked as a risk, while everything the campaign produces is within this epic's control.\n- Define the validation matrix: the supported model set, functional pass/fail criteria per model, and the performance parity baselines measured against the productized CUDA runtime builds.\n- Execute vLLM serving validation on ROCm for every model in the supported model set, using upstream ROCm-enabled vLLM builds.\n- Measure performance parity data per model against the CUDA baseline.\n- Publish the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance parity data, and a recommended go/no-go productization scope for each validated model.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation plan exists that enumerates the supported model set, the functional pass/fail criteria, and the performance parity baselines against the CUDA runtime builds.\n- The campaign report is published with functional validation results for every model in the supported model set.\n- The campaign report includes performance parity data per model, measured against the CUDA baseline on comparable hardware.\n- The campaign report states a recommended go/no-go productization scope for each validated model.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage — the validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, and producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Hardware access (procurement or partner-lab) is unresolved and controlled by parties outside the strategy; it may delay the campaign but does not change the campaign's deliverables.\n- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; the campaign validates against the upstream ROCm builds available at execution time.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43356,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b87630fa8d6650ba","agent_id":"aa34f687da752a1c0","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"9cde1f86-c4ee-4c4b-be18-359c05d18170","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:37:04.224Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
