{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f7eaadcb-e41d-4c10-b34f-efcf1c42407c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b4d0212aff11368","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-dvla9gvh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by the validation campaign, as an additional runtime variant alongside the existing CUDA builds. It delivers the midstream ROCm runtime image and the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime resources that make the runtime deployable through KServe InferenceServices on AMD Instinct nodes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and maintain the vLLM ROCm runtime image as a new image variant in the existing vLLM midstream repo (the repo is already onboarded; no new repo creation is needed).\n- Productize the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime resources for the ROCm vLLM runtime, covering exactly the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Build the ROCm runtime image from a supported upstream ROCm base aligned to the platform release train.\n- Validate KServe InferenceServices deploying and serving with the ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct nodes — KServe itself requires no code change for this strategy, so this is validation of a passive component rather than KServe development.\n- Build the image through the platform build pipeline (Konflux); the pipeline onboarding for the ROCm image variant runs in parallel with this epic, and this epic's completion is gated by a green pipeline run rather than by a dependency on the pipeline work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The vLLM ROCm runtime image is built and green through the platform build pipeline (Konflux).\n- ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime resources for the ROCm vLLM runtime are productized for exactly the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n- A KServe InferenceService using the ROCm vLLM runtime deploys and serves inference requests on AMD Instinct hardware.\n- The ROCm vLLM runtime ships as a supported runtime variant in a platform release, alongside (not replacing) the existing CUDA runtime builds.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): full coverage — a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n- This epic also carries the validation of KServe (listed as an affected component with no code change implied), per the third acceptance criterion.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Scope is gated on the validation campaign outcome: if fewer models clear than expected, productization narrows to the cleared set; if no model clears, productization is halted and the outcome is reported back to the strategy.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and may not align with platform release trains; a supported upstream base that is not release-train-aligned delays the release but does not change this epic's scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43356,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b87630fa8d6650ba","agent_id":"aa34f687da752a1c0","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"a62cae95-bef2-44e9-b96a-04c24f041cc5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:37:11.211Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
