{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f7eaadcb-e41d-4c10-b34f-efcf1c42407c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ba3ddd080b6b4f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-dvla9gvh/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for PyTorchJob\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic enables PyTorch training on ROCm for jobs run through the Training Operator: PyTorchJob workloads executing on AMD Instinct nodes with ROCm-enabled PyTorch training images, in single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies, admitted through the platform's queueing layer.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Support PyTorchJob execution on AMD Instinct nodes using ROCm-enabled PyTorch training images (single-GPU and multi-GPU topologies).\n- Validate the job lifecycle for ROCm-based PyTorchJobs (creation, run to completion, status reporting, cleanup).\n- Validate multi-GPU distributed training jobs on ROCm end to end, admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota configured (the quota configuration itself is delivered by the queueing workstream; this epic validates the training jobs against it).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob runs to completion on AMD Instinct nodes using a ROCm-enabled PyTorch image.\n- A multi-GPU distributed PyTorchJob runs to completion on AMD Instinct nodes.\n- Multi-GPU PyTorchJobs are admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota handling, using the queueing layer's AMD GPU quota configuration.\n- Job conditions and status are reported correctly for ROCm-based PyTorchJobs, consistent with existing GPU-backed jobs.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): training side — PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware; the availability of dedicated nodes is controlled by parties outside the strategy (shared constraint with th