strators configure queues for AMD Instinct capacity and how users request AMD GPUs.\n48\t- Any platform prerequisites or constraints for AMD GPU nodes, stated at the level the implementation work validated.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Documentation topics state the supported AMD hardware and driver prerequisites.\n53\t- Documentation states the validated model list, matching the scope cleared by the validation campaign.\n54\t- Documentation covers PyTorch ROCm training support, including single- and multi-GPU jobs and Kueue admission with amd.com/gpu quota.\n55\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented and validated capabilities (serving runtime, build pipeline, training, quota handling) before publication.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-4 (P2): full coverage — documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n60\t\n61\t## Notes\n62\t\n63\t- The strategy names no documentation owner; this epic is assigned to the serving team as the strategy's primary owner. Content spans both the serving and training areas, so technical reviewers should include the training/queueing team.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b04dfde947081c54","agent_id":"a75bd94d3d7d66008","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"b6ce710a-efc2-45f9-a629-db464c43b462","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:25.176Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-828a8bf4d6813bbe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
