he existing CUDA variants.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-2 (P0) — enabling coverage: this epic provides the build-pipeline leg of the productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime. It runs in parallel with the runtime productization work; their coupling is expressed as the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on that epic, not as a dependency between them.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-844c1cb1c17d805c","agent_id":"a77dadb429187cf0f","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"49be2af3-e4ab-490a-a1f2-bd04a2db3f28","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:47:37.693Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a810472b748d9a71","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
