Instinct nodes.\n45\t- Multi-GPU PyTorchJobs are admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota handling, using the queueing layer's AMD GPU quota configuration.\n46\t- Job conditions and status are reported correctly for ROCm-based PyTorchJobs, consistent with existing GPU-backed jobs.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-3 (P1): training side — PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs.\n51\t\n52\t## Risks\n53\t\n54\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware; the availability of dedicated nodes is controlled by parties outside the strategy (shared constraint with the serving validation campaign) and may delay validation but does not change this epic's deliverables.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-844c1cb1c17d805c","agent_id":"a77dadb429187cf0f","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"d4ff5a31-06c4-4d60-b46e-96c3049ee954","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:47:38.396Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-947c4592f14a8057","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
