 admission works for multi-GPU jobs requesting amd.com/gpu.\n45\t- Quota exhaustion for amd.com/gpu leaves workloads pending (not failed), consistent with existing GPU quota behavior.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (P1): queueing side — single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks\n52\t\n53\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware; the availability of dedicated nodes is controlled by parties outside the strategy (shared constraint with the serving validation campaign) and may delay validation but does not change this epic's deliverables.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-844c1cb1c17d805c","agent_id":"a77dadb429187cf0f","session_id":"c382ed88-b964-4c48-b2ae-a143f546fdbd","uuid":"8db44063-2ead-4949-ba50-e586cb0ea0ec","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:47:40.785Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0ac6b2ad72293d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
